% Small open economy with forward-looking investment (IRIS / irispie syntax).
%
% Monthly, linear, percent deviations from the steady state. The external
% variables follow the paths of the TVAR's generalized impulse responses: they
% enter as anticipated shocks known from the impact month on, so agents see the
% whole path after the surprise (rational expectations for a one-time shock).
%
% Confidence enters through a single parameter, phi: the responsiveness of
% investment to the expected return on capital (real options under
% uncertainty). Everything else is common to both regimes.

!transition-variables
    "Real GDP (constant prices)"                     y,
    "Private consumption"                            c,
    "Private investment"                             i,
    "Export volume"                                  x,
    "Expected discounted export price"               qp,
    "Expected discounted demand"                     qy,
    "Real fiscal revenues"                           rev,
    "Export price index"                             p,
    "Foreign demand (China industrial production)"   yf

!anticipated-shocks
    "Export price path"                              e_p,
    "Foreign demand path"                            e_yf

!parameters
    w_c, w_i, w_x, eta, h, mpc, chi, beta, rho_i, phi, a_p, a_y, tau_p, tau_y

!transition-equations
    "GDP at constant prices: domestic value added of spending plus exports"
    y = w_c*c + w_i*i + w_x*x;

    "Export volumes respond to foreign demand, not to export prices"
    x = eta*yf;

    "Consumption: partial adjustment to income and to the households' share of the price windfall"
    c = h*c[-1] + (1 - h)*(mpc*y + chi*p);

    "Expected discounted export price"
    qp = beta*qp[+1] + (1 - beta)*p;

    "Expected discounted demand"
    qy = beta*qy[+1] + (1 - beta)*y;

    "Investment: partial adjustment to the expected return, scaled by confidence"
    i = rho_i*i[-1] + (1 - rho_i)*phi*(a_p*qp + a_y*qy);

    "Fiscal revenues: commodity taxes and activity"
    rev = tau_p*p + tau_y*y;

    p = e_p;
    yf = e_yf;
